# Pulled/derived FAAB-pool data - large (combined-training-table.parquet
# alone is well over GitHub's 100MB per-file push limit outright) and the
# three raw pulled-data files can't be regenerated if lost (real bid/roster
# history scraped from other people's public ESPN leagues at a point in
# time). Not in git; instead they're release assets on the "faab-data"
# GitHub release - `python -m tools.faab_history.fetch_release_data` pulls
# what a normal pipeline run needs, `--all` also gets the raw inputs to
# rebuild the training table from scratch via build_training_table.py.
tools/faab_history/combined-training-table.parquet
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-bids-raw.json
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-bids.json
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-rostered-by-week.json
*.bak

